<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25126" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭtĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		eo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				going</i>, <i>walking</i>, <i>travelling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">itiones crebrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 5, 8, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de obviam itione ita faciam, ut suades,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 11, 16, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaeris quod cogitem de obviam itione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 50, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reditum ac domum itionem dari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Div. 1, 32, 68</span></i>
			.</div>
